# Inventory Management System for End User Equipment

## Challenge Solution | Spring Boot MVC | Fully Offline Windows Application

---

## 📌 Overview

This system addresses Airtel's challenge of lacking a centralized system to track end-user devices (laptops, desktops, mobile phones). It provides a **fully offline, Windows‑based** desktop application with a local database, ensuring accurate asset tracking, accountability, and comprehensive reporting even without internet connectivity.

---

## ✨ Features (Complete Scope)

| Requirement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| Asset registration (device details, specifications) | ✅ Add new asset form |
| Assignment & ownership tracking | ✅ Issue asset to employee (name + department) |
| Condition monitoring | ✅ New / Good / Faulty |
| Issue and return management | ✅ Issue date, return date, automatic status update |
| Comprehensive reporting | ✅ By department, device type, condition, status, date range |
| Search & filtering | ✅ By device type, department, condition, status |
| Audit history | ✅ Every create, update, issue, return, delete is logged |
| Fully offline | ✅ H2 file‑based database (no external server) |
| Windows executable | ✅ Run as JAR with `.bat` launcher |

---

## 🛠️ Technology Stack

- **Backend:** Spring Boot 2.7.18
- **Frontend:** Thymeleaf + HTML/CSS
- **Database:** H2 (file‑based, embedded)
- **Security:** Spring Security (in‑memory authentication)
- **Build Tool:** Maven
- **Java Version:** 17

